%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Course Introduction}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Welcome To AI Mastery}
}

This learning universe teaches Artificial Intelligence from beginner concepts to advanced projects.

By the end of this course you will:

\begin{itemize}
\item Understand AI and Machine Learning
\item Build predictive models
\item Train neural networks
\item Deploy AI systems
\item Create portfolio projects
\end{itemize}

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aircAruvnKk}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Lesson 1: Introduction to Machine Learning}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={What is Machine Learning?}
}

Machine Learning enables computers to learn patterns from data without explicit programming.

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ukzFI9rgwfU}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
print("Hello Machine Learning")
},
expectedoutput={
Hello Machine Learning
}
}

\quiz{
question={Machine Learning is a subset of?},
options={Artificial Intelligence|Database Systems|Operating Systems|Networking},
answer={Artificial Intelligence}
}

\project{
title={AI Career Roadmap},
description={Create a roadmap describing your AI learning journey.}
}

\resource{
type={pdf},
title={ML Beginner Guide},
url={https://example.com/ml-guide.pdf}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Lesson 2: Linear Regression}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Linear Regression Fundamentals}
}

Linear Regression predicts numerical values using relationships between variables.

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nk2CQITm_eo}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
import numpy as np

x=np.array([1,2,3,4,5])
y=np.array([2,4,6,8,10])

print(x)
print(y)
},
expectedoutput={
[1 2 3 4 5]
[2 4 6 8 10]
}
}

\quiz{
question={Linear Regression is mainly used for?},
options={Regression|Classification|Clustering|Security},
answer={Regression}
}

\project{
title={House Price Prediction},
description={Build a model to predict house prices using historical data.}
}

\resource{
type={github},
title={Regression Code Repository},
url={https://github.com}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Lesson 3: Classification}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Classification Algorithms}
}

Classification predicts categories instead of continuous values.

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qJaSmvhxi8}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
labels=["Cat","Dog","Bird"]
print(labels)
},
expectedoutput={
['Cat', 'Dog', 'Bird']
}
}

\quiz{
question={Classification predicts?},
options={Categories|Prices|Revenue|Time},
answer={Categories}
}

\project{
title={Spam Email Detector},
description={Create a classifier that detects spam emails.}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Lesson 4: Neural Networks}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Introduction to Neural Networks}
}

Neural Networks are inspired by biological neurons and power modern AI.

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aircAruvnKk}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
import tensorflow as tf
print(tf.__version__)
},
expectedoutput={
TensorFlow Version
}
}

\quiz{
question={Neural Networks are heavily used in?},
options={Deep Learning|Word Processing|Networking|Databases},
answer={Deep Learning}
}

\project{
title={Image Classification Model},
description={Build a CNN to classify handwritten digits.}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Final Capstone Project}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\project{
