}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
% LESSON 1
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Introduction to Artificial Intelligence}
}

Artificial Intelligence is the science of building systems that can reason, learn, and make decisions.

AI is everywhere:

- ChatGPT
- Self Driving Cars
- Medical Diagnosis
- Recommendation Systems
- Robotics

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JMUxmLyrhSk}
}

\video{
type={local},
url={/uploads/videos/intro-ai.mp4}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
print("Welcome to AI")
},
expectedoutput={
Welcome to AI
}
}

\quiz{
question={What does AI stand for?},
optionA={Artificial Intelligence},
optionB={Automated Internet},
optionC={Advanced Interface},
optionD={Artificial Input},
correct={A},
explanation={AI stands for Artificial Intelligence.}
}

\project{
title={AI Career Roadmap},
colab={https://colab.research.google.com/},
instructions={Explore AI domains and create your own roadmap.}
}

\resource{
type={pdf},
title={AI Beginner Guide},
url={https://arxiv.org/pdf/1708.05866.pdf}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
% LESSON 2
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Machine Learning Fundamentals}
}

Machine Learning allows systems to learn patterns from data.

Three types:

- Supervised Learning
- Unsupervised Learning
- Reinforcement Learning

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GwIo3gDZCVQ}
}

\video{
type={local},
url={/uploads/videos/ml-basics.mp4}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
import numpy as np

x=np.array([1,2,3,4])
print(x)
},
expectedoutput={
[1 2 3 4]
}
}

\quiz{
question={Machine Learning is a subset of?},
optionA={Networking},
optionB={Artificial Intelligence},
optionC={Databases},
optionD={Operating Systems},
correct={B},
explanation={Machine Learning is a subset of AI.}
}

\project{
title={Predict House Prices},
colab={https://colab.research.google.com/},
instructions={Build a simple regression model.}
}

\resource{
type={github},
title={Machine Learning Repository},
url={https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
% LESSON 3
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Python for Machine Learning}
}

Python is the most popular language for AI.

Libraries:

- NumPy
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-Learn
- TensorFlow

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rfscVS0vtbw}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
numbers=[1,2,3,4,5]
print(sum(numbers))
},
expectedoutput={
15
}
}

\quiz{
question={Which library is used for arrays?},
optionA={TensorFlow},
optionB={NumPy},
optionC={Flask},
optionD={Django},
correct={B},
explanation={NumPy provides multidimensional arrays.}
}

\project{
title={Python ML Toolkit},
colab={https://colab.research.google.com/},
instructions={Build utility functions for ML workflows.}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
% LESSON 4
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Deep Learning and Neural Networks}
}

Deep Learning uses neural networks with multiple layers.

Formula:

Output = Σ(Weight × Input)

Concepts:

- Neurons
- Weights
- Bias
- Activation Functions

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aircAruvnKk}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
weights=[0.2,0.5,0.8]
inputs=[1,2,3]

result=0

for i in range(len(weights)):
 result+=weights[i]*inputs[i]

print(result)
},
expectedoutput={
3.6
}
}

\quiz{
question={Deep Learning uses?},
optionA={Neural Networks},
optionB={Databases},
optionC={HTML},
optionD={Networking},
correct={A},
explanation={Deep Learning is built on Neural Networks.}
}

\project{
title={Neural Network From Scratch},
colab={https://colab.research.google.com/},
instructions={Implement a single neuron model.}
}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
% LESSON 5
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\lesson{
title={Computer Vision}
}

Computer Vision enables machines to understand images.

Applications:

- Face Recognition
- Object Detection
- Medical Imaging
- Autonomous Vehicles

\video{
type={youtube},
url={https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WQeoO7MI0Bs}
}

\practice{
language={python},
startercode={
import cv2
print(cv2.__version__)
},
expectedoutput={
OpenCV Version
}
}

\quiz{
question={Computer Vision works with?},
optionA={Images and Videos},
optionB={Databases},
optionC={Networks},
optionD={Operating Systems},
correct={A},
explanation={Computer Vision analyzes visual data.}
}

\project{
title={Face Detection App},
colab={https://colab.research.google.com/},
instructions={Build a face detector using OpenCV.}
}

\resource{
type={github},
title={OpenCV Repository},
url={https://github.com/opencv/opencv}
}

\end{document}

